# Copy to .env and fill in for anything beyond local development.
# Never commit the real .env file, and never hardcode a private key in
# source (hardhat.config.js, deploy.js, registerCredential.js all read
# these from the environment for exactly this reason).

# --- Local development (default) ---
# Nothing needs to be set here. `localhost` network uses the Hardhat node's
# own well-known test accounts, which is fine ONLY because that node is
# local and not reachable by anyone else.

# --- Any real network (testnet/mainnet) ---
# RPC endpoint for the target network (e.g. an Infura/Alchemy URL).
# SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=

# Private key of the account that deploys the contract and becomes its
# owner (accreditation authority). Fund this address with enough native
# token to cover deployment gas. NEVER the local Hardhat test mnemonic.
# DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Private key of the account the backend uses to call registerCredential().
# Must be accredited on-chain first (the deployer is auto-accredited; grant
# this one too via registry.accreditIssuer(address) if it's different).
# ISSUER_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Overrides the address auto-read from deployed.json, if needed.
# CONTRACT_ADDRESS=

# Overrides who becomes the contract's owner at deploy time (defaults to
# the deployer's own address). Setting this to a Safe multisig address
# instead of a plain EOA is how the registry avoids being governed by a
# single private key — see the "Governance: single key vs a Safe
# multisig" section this same reasoning is documented under in full,
# below scripts/deploySafe.js's own header comment or wherever this
# project's README/docs currently cover it. Becomes the PERMANENT owner
# the instant deployment mines, with no confirmation step of its own (see
# deploy.js's own code-existence + OWNER_ADDRESS_CONFIRMED check) — this
# is NOT the same two-step safety Ownable2Step gives a LATER
# transferOwnership() call.
# OWNER_ADDRESS=

# Required alongside OWNER_ADDRESS (deploy.js refuses without it) — an
# explicit acknowledgment that OWNER_ADDRESS is about to become the
# contract's permanent owner, checked on a block explorer / against
# deployed-safe.json first. Exists specifically so a copy-paste typo in
# OWNER_ADDRESS can't silently misconfigure the registry irrecoverably.
# OWNER_ADDRESS_CONFIRMED=

# --- Safe multisig (scripts/deploySafe.js, scripts/transferRegistryOwnershipToSafe.js) ---
# Comma-separated list of the REAL signers' addresses for the Safe that
# should own the registry — e.g.
# SAFE_OWNERS=0xAbc...,0xDef...,0x123...
# Required on any network other than localhost/hardhat — deploySafe.js
# refuses to deploy a Safe "owned" by its own local demo accounts
# anywhere reachable by anyone but you. IMPORTANT: this script only ever
# needs these ADDRESSES, never the matching private keys — a real Safe is
# created by its actual owners themselves (via app.safe.global, connecting
# their own wallets, or each running their own signing session), not by
# handing one script/one machine enough keys to act alone. Generating
# "production" signer keys FOR the intended owners defeats the entire
# point of a multisig; don't do that here or anywhere else in this
# project.
# SAFE_OWNERS=

# How many of SAFE_OWNERS must confirm a transaction before it executes.
# Default 2 (i.e. 2-of-3 if SAFE_OWNERS has 3 addresses) if unset.
# SAFE_THRESHOLD=

# Only needed by transferRegistryOwnershipToSafe.js, and only if
# deployed-safe.json (written by deploySafe.js) isn't present or doesn't
# match the Safe you mean — overrides which Safe address ownership is
# being transferred to.
# SAFE_ADDRESS=
